<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Omnichannel retail</h2>
<p>Omnichannel Retail readiness starts with provable consent records and instant post-checkout suppression across each app running omnichannel retail sends. Omnichannel Retail audiences forgive plain creative; they do not forgive promos sent mid-refund or right after checkout.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Suppress omnichannel retail marketing entirely until consent is documented</td><td>Without omnichannel retail consent proof, marketing has no legal footing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>First omnichannel retail touches teach and reassure before selling</td><td>Omnichannel Retail margin suffers when discounts arrive first</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Omnichannel Retail cart reminder first; earn the discount decision</td><td>Guards omnichannel retail margin while intent peaks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Pause omnichannel retail promos; switch to post-purchase teaching</td><td>Keeps omnichannel retail buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Freeze omnichannel retail promos until refund or return closes</td><td>Open omnichannel retail cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic omnichannel retail non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Shields omnichannel retail sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold omnichannel retail texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>Omnichannel Retail SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Omnichannel Retail B2B routing stays account-specific</td><td>Omnichannel Retail retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Omnichannel Retail automation skips unverified domains first</td><td>Omnichannel Retail bounces from junk signups hurt inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Omnichannel Retail QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Omnichannel Retail reporting stays clean without test noise</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>No bespoke omnichannel retail track for competitor signals</td><td>Omnichannel Retail one-offs breed audit gaps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Re-permission legacy omnichannel retail lists pre-automation</td><td>Timestamp-less omnichannel retail consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Omnichannel retail</h2>
<p>Attributed revenue is not profit for omnichannel retail. A self-funding omnichannel retail program survives a full cost model: subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, capture tooling, templates, agency time, and every point of omnichannel retail discount margin. For omnichannel retail, a stack at fifteen percent of attributed margin needs simplification first, optimization second.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. Free tiers ration contacts, sends, branching, or support — confirm which ceiling binds your omnichannel retail plan first.</p>
